# Releasing Tidewater @release
{
    @meta {
        type: skill

        sdoc-version: 0.2
    }

    @about {
        How to cut a tidewater release, from the freeze to the announcement, and what must hold before the tag. Use it whenever you prepare, tag or publish a release, including a patch release.
    }

    # Before You Start @before
    {
        A release needs a clean `main`, a green build on it, and a free reference host for the long-running tests. Book the host, `soak-3`, a day ahead in the team calendar: the tests occupy it for six hours.
    }

    # Steps @steps
    {
        {[#]
            - Freeze and branch
            {
                Announce the freeze in the team channel, then create `release/vX.Y.Z` from `main`. From here on only fixes for the release land on the branch, each also merged to `main`.
            }
            - Run the soak test
            {
                On `soak-3`, run `make soak VERSION=vX.Y.Z` from the release branch. It runs the long-running tests for six hours and fails if any figure misses its budget by more than 10 percent, or if any log truncation happens during the run. A failed soak test stops the release until it passes on a rerun after the fix.
            }
            - Bump the format version if the on-disk format changed
            {
                If any change since the last release alters what is written to disk, increase `TIDEWATER_FORMAT_VERSION` in `src/format.go` by one, add the new version to the on-disk format table in the architecture, and add a test that opens a database written by the previous release. If the format did not change, leave the constant alone.
            }
            - Write the changelog
            {
                Add a section for the release to `CHANGELOG.md`, listing every changed default, renamed metric and new error under its own heading, since applications depend on all three.
            }
            - Tag
            {
                Tag the release commit with a signed tag, `git tag -s vX.Y.Z`, using the release key. An unsigned tag is rejected by the module proxy mirror the project publishes to.
            }
            - Publish and announce
            {
                Run `make publish VERSION=vX.Y.Z`, which pushes the tag and warms the module proxy, then post the changelog section in the team channel.
            }
        }
    }

    # Patch Releases @patch-releases
    {
        A patch release follows the same steps from an existing `release/vX.Y` branch, with two exceptions: the soak test may be shortened to two hours with `SOAK_HOURS=2` when the fix does not touch the write path, and the format version never changes in a patch release.
    }
}
